Subject: [M150-LTS] Do not reuse non-CORS StyleImage data with a CORS request

The StyleImageCache does not record the CORS status of the cached
image content. Loading an image as a background with no CORS
requirement caches the image, and a subsequent request for the
same image as a CSS mask-image request for a CORS image will
return the non-CORS result from the cache.

Fix it by checking the origin status of the cached image and
rejecting it when its status is inadequate for the request.

(cherry picked from commit 25df6183505df2d433fb117d5a1101ab0df9a399)

